   "id": "korea-rebound-hynix-buyback",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Seoul stocks rally over 4% as SK hynix steps up share buybacks",
   "when": "Fri 27 Nov · close in Seoul",
   "what": "KOSPI rose 204 points, or 4.34%, to 4,915.68. Gainers beat losers 781 to 109. Samsung Electronics gained 4.55% to 179,100 won and SK hynix 5.41% to 1.11 million won. Foreign investors bought a net 1.13 trillion won. The won firmed to about 1,338 per dollar. Authorities plan a meeting next week on enlarging the 10 trillion won stabilisation fund. SK hynix doubled its daily buyback orders to about 700,000 shares, saying its stock is undervalued. The shares are still about 63% below their June high.",
   "why": "SCBKEQTG and EWY are mostly Samsung and SK hynix exposure, so a chip-led rebound matters most for them. The rally rests on hopes of support, and an analyst quoted said gains may stay limited until new money arrives. Your SCBKEQTG NAV is dated 24 Nov; the market fell about 5.9% by 26 Nov and then rose 4.3% on Friday.",
